nodecode-zalo is a rewrite of moken627-hub's moken627-hub/hermes-plugin-zalo:

  https://github.com/moken627-hub/hermes-plugin-zalo
  commit 5a989368d0877c930e76fcc75ea125e7af7ea872
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Moken (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is the repository root of that commit (plugin.yaml,
__init__.py, zalo/adapter.py). What was carried over: the Bot API wire
(https://bot-api.zaloplatforms.com/bot<token>/<method>, `getUpdates` in long
poll, `sendMessage`, `getMe`, `kickGroupMember`, `pinGroupMessage`,
`createPoll`), the response shape (`ok` / `result`, with one update object or
an array), the admission rule this cell keeps with `allowed_users` and
`allow_all`, the six slash commands it answers itself in Vietnamese, the
2000-character chunking, and the markdown stripping that turns an answer into
the plain text Zalo shows. The token is scrubbed from any error the cell
reports, as the original scrubs it from its httpx errors.

What was left out, and why: webhook mode, because a cell reaches the API by
long polling and needs no listener of its own; the anti-spam rate limiter, the
warn/report bookkeeping, the welcome messages and the name triggers, which are
in-memory maps and JSON files of the original's runtime rather than anything
Zalo asked for; the per-group settings, chat-history and CRM stores under the
Hermes home, of which a session per chat is the Nodecode form; and the
`hermes gateway setup` wizard and `hermes pairing approve` flow, whose answers
the section, /settings and /zalo give here. LICENSE is the repository's
LICENSE, unchanged; it carries a third-party MIT section for the Hermes Agent
UI strings the original mirrors.
